.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-E2FSPROGS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-e2fsprogs ,
.Nm chattr ,
.Nm fsck ,
.Nm lsattr
.Nd BusyBox file system attribute and check tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm chattr
.Op Fl R
.Op Fl v Ar VERSION
.Op Fl p Ar PROJID
.Op Ar -+=AacDdijsStTu
.Ar FILE ...
.Nm fsck
.Op Fl ANPRTV
.Op Fl t Ar FSTYPE
.Op Ar FS_OPTS
.Op Ar BLOCKDEV
.Ar ...
.Nm lsattr
.Op Fl Radlpv
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the e2fsprogs applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width chattr
.It Nm chattr
Change ext2 file attributes.
The kernel stores the ones ext2 lets a user change and enforces two, as
Linux does:
.Ql i ,
immutable, which refuses a write, a truncation, a removal, a rename, a
link and a change of the attributes, to root too, and
.Ql a ,
append-only, which also refuses those but an append.
Only a privileged caller sets or clears either, and the owner the
others.
.Fl v
and
.Fl p
fail with
.Ql Inappropriate ioctl for device .
.It Nm fsck
Check and repair file systems by running
.Pa fsck.TYPE
for the selected file system type.
The recovery system's ext2 checker is the separate e2fsprogs program
.Xr e2fsck 8 .
.It Nm lsattr
List ext2 file attributes.
On an ext2 volume the kernel reports each inode's flags and, for
.Fl v ,
its generation.
A file of another file system, and
.Fl p ,
fail with
.Ql Inappropriate ioctl for device .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss chattr
.Bl -tag -width "-v NUM"
.It Fl R
Recurse into directories.
.It Fl v Ar NUM
Set the version or generation number.
.It Fl p Ar NUM
Set the project number.
.El
.Ss fsck
.Bl -tag -width "-A"
.It Fl A
Read
.Pa /etc/fstab
and check all file systems.
.It Fl N
Show what would be done without executing checkers.
.It Fl P
With
.Fl A ,
do not check the root file system separately before the others.
.It Fl R
With
.Fl A ,
skip the root file system.
.It Fl T
Suppress the startup title.
.It Fl V
Produce verbose output.
.El
.Ss lsattr
.Bl -tag -width "-R"
.It Fl R
Recurse into directories.
.It Fl a
Include names beginning with a period.
.It Fl d
List directory names instead of their contents.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/fstab
.It Pa /etc/fstab
File systems to check with
.Nm fsck Fl A .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr e2fsck 8
